&lt;p&gt;This is a rare opportunity to join Warp at a pivotal moment in our growth. You would directly help scale the go-to-market motion for Warp Factories, our platform for helping engineering organizations automate major parts of the software development lifecycle with AI agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As enterprises move from individual developers using AI to deploying agents across the software development lifecycle, they need infrastructure to build, run, and manage these systems at scale. Warp Factories takes a platform approach: rather than prescribing a single agent, model, or workflow, we give engineering organizations the infrastructure to build software factories around their own environments, tools, and requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Strategic Account Executive, you&#39;ll work with some of the world&#39;s largest and most sophisticated engineering organizations to help them make this transition. You&#39;ll own complex, high-value opportunities from initial discovery through technical evaluation, FDE-led deployments, executive alignment, and commercial close.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join a team with strong product momentum and an established enterprise customer base, while still having the opportunity to shape how we bring a new category of infrastructure to market. We&#39;re looking for someone who wants to build: someone who is excited to develop new use cases, work closely with customers and our product team, and help define what great enterprise adoption of Warp Factories looks like.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle for strategic enterprise accounts, from initial engagement and discovery through technical evaluation, procurement, and close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sell Warp Factories to senior engineering, AI, platform, and technology leaders, helping customers understand how agentic software development can transform engineering velocity, cost, and operating models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help customers identify high-value opportunities for software factories and translate broad AI initiatives into concrete deployments with measurable business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position Warp&#39;s infrastructure-first approach and help customers understand how they can build and operate software factories without locking themselves into a single agent, model, or workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structure and sell FDE-led engagements where Warp works alongside customers to design, deploy, and operationalize their first software factories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Forward Deployed Engineers, Solutions Engineers, Product, and Engineering throughout complex technical evaluations and deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate multi-threaded enterprise deals involving engineering leadership, AI/platform teams, security, procurement, legal, and executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build compelling business cases connecting technical outcomes - including increased automation, engineering throughput, and cost efficiency - to executive priorities and ROI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop champions and executive relationships across strategic accounts and create paths from initial deployments to broad enterprise adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Warp&#39;s strategic sales motion by helping refine qualification, messaging, use cases, commercial structures, and deployment playbooks based on what you&#39;re seeing in the market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
