&lt;li&gt;6-10+ years of enterprise software sales experience, with a track record of closing complex, high-value deals with large organizations, ideally in a fast-paced startup environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling highly technical products to engineering, infrastructure, platform, or AI organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong consultative selling skills, including the ability to uncover new use cases, navigate technical evaluations, and build compelling business cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to create executive-level urgency around emerging technologies and new ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to engage credibly with everyone from hands-on engineering leaders to CTOs, CIOs, and other C-suite executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical curiosity. You don&#39;t need to be an engineer, but you should be comfortable going deep on AI agents, developer workflows, infrastructure, security, and software architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity and change. You take ownership, move quickly, and enjoy helping shape the path forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder mentality. You&#39;re excited to help evolve the sales motion, develop new use cases, and work closely with customers and internal teams as the market develops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
